## What was built
**7 Swift files** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/`, ~1,250 lines) mirroring the gold-standard `RouteEfficiencyPage` architecture:
- `TripListPageModel.swift` — `@MainActor @Observable` model + `Trip`/`Vehicle` types + `TripListDataSource` seam (web hooks `useTrips`/`useSelectedVehicle` kept) + phase enum + all web `useMemo` derivations
- `TripListFormat.swift` — display-boundary SI converters via the shared `Units` facade (P1/S5)
- `TripListPageModel.Sample.swift` — sample/empty/failing data sources for the 3 states
- `TripListPage.swift` — adaptive scaffold, header, phase switch, range control, skeleton
- `TripListPage.Panels.swift` — 4 stat cards + All-Trips list + per-trip rows
- `TripListPage.Charts.swift` — `TSChartContainer` + `TSBarChart` (P3 Swift Charts, no WKWebView) + CSV/JSON export
- `TripsRouteRegistration.swift` — `.trips` host registration (wired into `TeslaSyncApp`)

Plus **22 `trips.*` i18n keys** (+`inProgress`) appended to `Localizable.xcstrings`, and **2 ledger rows**.

